==Old English==

===Etymology===
From an earlier form ''[[hlafweard|hlāfweard]]'', from Germanic ''*hlaibhward-'', from ''*hlaibh'' ‘bread’ ( > ''[[hlaf|hlāf]]'') + ''*ward'' ( > ''[[weard]]'').

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈhlɑːvord/, [ˈɬɑːvɔrd]|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{Latinx|'''hlāford'''}} {{m}} (''plural'' {{Latinx|'''[[hlafordas|hlāfordas]]'''}})

# [[lord]], master of servants
# male head of a household

====Descendants====
* English: [[lord]]
* Scots: [[laird]]

